{"nodes": [{"id": "recovered_prediction_delta_session_40_document", "label": "PREDICTION-DELTA (s40 item 3)", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-DELTA-SESSION-40.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_prediction_delta_session_40_delta_decomposition", "label": "The Delta decomposition: D(n,l) = -1/(2n^2) + Delta(n,l)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-DELTA-SESSION-40.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The hydrogenic reference is not fitted and contains no parameter, so Delta is the entire departure of the channel from a fully screened core \u2014 which is what penetration names."}, {"id": "recovered_prediction_delta_session_40_non_penetrating_floor", "label": "PD-4: the non-penetrating floor, register 1255's centrifugal gate restated on Delta", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-DELTA-SESSION-40.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "recovered_prediction_delta_session_40_pd_7_penetration_inversion", "label": "PD-7: the 4s-before-3d inversion is entirely a penetration effect", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-DELTA-SESSION-40.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "At Z=19 the hydrogenic term prefers 3d by 0.02431 and loses, because 4s wins on Delta (-0.11649 against -0.00251) \u2014 so both terms are load-bearing and the decomposition is not a relabelling."}, {"id": "recovered_prediction_delta_session_40_pd_5_4f_collapse_discontinuity", "label": "PD-5: the f collapse is a discontinuity in Delta and not in D", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "recovered/PREDICTION-DELTA-SESSION-40.md", "source_location": null, "source_url":